  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a3d2b5e5b8bd75781820de5be38f0970, type: 3}
  m_Name: ExhibitData_microscope
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ExhibitData
  exhibitName: THE MICROSCOPE
  pages:
  - "Did you know there is an entire invisible world\nhiding all around you on your
    hands, in the air,\neven on this very panel?\n \nIn the 1670s, a Dutch cloth
    merchant named\nAntonie van Leeuwenhoek built tiny powerful lenses\nand looked
    at a drop of pond water.\nHe saw creatures swimming around in it!\nHe called
    them \"little animalcules\" \u2014\nand he was the first human ever to see living
    bacteria."
  - "Leeuwenhoek had no science degree.\nHe was just incredibly curious and incredibly
    patient.\nHe spent years grinding lenses by hand\nto make them sharper and more
    powerful.\n \nBecause of the microscope, doctors learned what\nreally causes
    diseases, and millions of lives were saved.\nAll from a curious man with a piece
    of glass\nand a drop of water. \U0001F52C"
  exhibitIllustration: {fileID: -4428912374758282309, guid: e06c96ed32622d55fbfb04266acd304a, type: 3}
  narratorClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 48256d534a2203d328e7e9b802daafbe, type: 3}
